  "findings": [
    "Explicit constructor stores its full unsigned-long color argument; default constructor stores all-one missing sentinel. Copy construction preserves all 32 bits. Explicit layer setter preserves its full color int on its non-sentinel layer branch. None of these paths normalizes the stored high byte."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Preservation does not establish the purpose of the high byte, its complete valid domain, alpha semantics, or reserved status. The existing graphics getter discards it before RGB consumption. No decoder or coverage change."
  ]
